==English==

===Etymology 1===
[[re-]] + [[cap]]

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|rē-kăpʹ}}, {{IPA|/riːˈkæp/|lang=en}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb|recaps|recapping|recapped}}

# To seal (something) again with a cap.
# To replace the [[worn]] [[tread]] on a [[tire]] by gluing a new outer portion.
#* {{quote-news|work=Kiplinger's Personal Finance|year=1957|Month=Aug|volume=11|number=8||title=Recap your old tires?|page=13|passage=Are '''recapped''' tires safe? This is obviously the thing to know before you consider buying recaps.}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A tire that has had new [[tread]] glued on.
#* {{quote-book|year=2008|title=Law for Business and Personal Use|isbn=0538445882|author=John Adamson|page=102|passage=As she did so, Stacy noted that the tire had been a '''recap'''—a tire created by gluing a new outer portion of tread onto the worn inner core of old tires.}}

===Etymology 2===
Shortened from [[recapitulate]]/[[recapitulation]]

====Pronunciation====
* {{qualifier|noun}} {{enPR|rēʹ-kăp}}, {{IPA|/ˈriːkæp/|lang=en}}
* {{qualifier|verb}} {{enPR|rē-kăpʹ|rēʹ-kăp}}, {{IPA|/riːˈkæp/|/ˈriːkæp/|lang=en}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[recapitulation]].

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|recapitulation}} [[summarisation]]/[[summarization]], [[summary]], [[summing-up]]

====Verb====
{{en-verb|recapp}}

# To [[recapitulate]].

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|recapitulate}} [[summarise]]/[[summarize]], [[sum up]]

===Etymology 3===
Shortened from [[recapitalization]]

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[leveraged]] [[recapitalization]] accomplished by increasing the [[debt]] to [[equity]] ratio.
#* {{quote-book|title=Merger Arbitrage: How to Profit from Event-Driven Arbitrage|author=Thomas Kirchner|year=2009|page=196|ISBN=0470508116|passage=A survey of private equity firms found that most firms are comfortable with a debt/equity ratio of 4:1 following a dividend '''recap'''.}}

